    "cause": "When the conveyance expansion board cooling fan (FM65) is active, an error detection signal is detected continuously for a specified period of time. Though the machine retries power feed several times, an error detection signal is detected continuously. Measures to take when alert occurs The main body and the option stop immediately. Estimated abnormal parts • Conveyance expansion board cooling fan (FM65) Correction Note ▪ The message \"Please call service\" is displayed on the panel. Solution 1. Prior check • Close the front door properly. (Check with the IO Check (25-20) of the front door sensor (PS001).) 2. Execute the IO Check (42-76) of the conveyance expansion board cooling fan (FM65). 3. When the result of the IO Check in the step 2 is normal, FM65 is not abnormal. Go on to step 5. For details of IO check results, refer to \"Table 1: Result check.\" 4. Check the connector connection between the conveyance drive board (CDB) and FM65, CN173 of CDB, CN498 of FM65, and the wiring. Then, repair it when there is any abnormality. 5. Rotate FM65 by hand, and repair it when there is any abnormality. 6. Replace FM65. Table 1: Result check Result check Normal Abnormal START Change 1→0 1 STOP Not care Not care Faulty part isolation DIPSW Control during the detachment",
