    "cause": "Rotation abnormality of the shutter motor/Rr3 is detected. Measures to take when alert occurs The main body and the option stop immediately. Estimated abnormal parts • PFU drive board (PFUDB) • Shutter motor/Rr3 (M43) • Shutter home sensor/Lw1 (PS47) Correction Note ▪ The message \"Please call service\" is displayed on the panel. Solution 1. Execute the IO Check (20-19) of the shutter motor/Rr3 (Lower tray) (PF 2nd tandem). 2. When the result of the IO Check in the step 1 is normal, M43 is not abnormal. Go on to the step 3. 3. Check the status of the sensor (0 or 1) in the IO Check (21-55) of the shutter home sensor/Lw1 (Lower tray) (PF 2nd tandem). 4. Execute the IO Check (20-19) of the shutter motor/Rr3 (Lower tray) (PF 2nd tandem) again. 5. Check the status of the sensor (0 or 1) in the IO Check (21-55) of the shutter home sensor/Lw1 (Lower tray) (PF 2nd tandem). If the status of the sensor changes from the status when you checked in the step 3 (from 0 to 1, or from 1 to 0), PS47 is not abnormal. Go on to the step 7. 6. Check the connector connection of CN123 of PFUDB, CN526 of M43, CN524 of PS47, CN528 of the relay connector, and the wiring. Then, repair it when there is any abnormality. 7. Replace PFUDB. 8. Replace M43. 9. Replace PS47. Faulty part isolation DIPSW Control during the detachment",
