    "code": "C-1480",
    "class": "Main body: Charging control unit abnormality",
    "cause": "An error detection signal of the charge control unit is detected continuously for a specified period of time. Though the machine retries power feed several times, an error detection signal is detected continuously. Measures to take when alert occurs The main body and the option stop immediately. Estimated abnormal parts • Charging roller assy • High voltage power supply/23 (HV23) Correction Note ▪ The message \"Please call service\" is displayed on the panel. Solution 1. Prior check • The charge control unit is installed properly. • Close the front door properly. (Check with the IO Check (25-20) of the front door sensor (PS001).) 2. Execute the IO Check (07-00) of the high voltage power supply/23 (HV23). 3. When the result of the IO Check in the step 2 is normal, HV23 is not abnormal. Go on to step 7. For details of IO check results, refer to \"Table 1: Result check.\" 4. Check the connector connection between the printer control board (PRCB) and HV23, CN155 of PRCB, CN289 (Relay connector), CN61 of HV23, and the wiring. Then, repair it when there is any abnormality. 5. Check the connector connection between the DC power supply/4 (DCPS/04) and HV23, CN208 (Relay connector), CN60 of HV23, and the wiring. Then repair it when there is any abnormality. 6. Replace the charging roller assy. 7. Replace HV23. Table 1: Result check Result check Normal Abnormal START Change 1→0 1 STOP Not care Not care Faulty part isolation DIPSW DIPSW35-7 Control during the detachment The charge control unit is unavailable.",
    "measure": "",
    "abnormal": "• Charging roller assy • High voltage power supply/23 (HV23)",
    "corr": "",
    "note": "▪ The message \"Please call service\" is displayed on the panel.",
    "solution": "1. Prior check • The charge control unit is installed properly. • Close the front door properly. (Check with the IO Check (25-20) of the front door sensor (PS001).) 2. Execute the IO Check (07-00) of the high voltage power supply/23 (HV23). 3. When the result of the IO Check in the step 2 is normal, HV23 is not abnormal. Go on to step 7. For details of IO check results, refer to \"Table 1: Result check.\" 4. Check the connector connection between the printer control board (PRCB) and HV23, CN155 of PRCB, CN289 (Relay connector), CN61 of HV23, and the wiring. Then, repair it when there is any abnormality. 5. Check the connector connection between the DC power supply/4 (DCPS/04) and HV23, CN208 (Relay connector), CN60 of HV23, and the wiring. Then repair it when there is any abnormality. 6. Replace the charging roller assy. 7. Replace HV23. Table 1: Result check Result check Normal Abnormal START Change 1→0 1 STOP Not care Not care",
    "isolate": "DIPSW35-7 Control during the detachment The charge control unit is unavailable.",
    "control": ""
