    "solution": "<When abnormality occurs during the Gamma Automatic Adjustment operation> 1. Perform the Beam Pitch Adjustment. 2. Perform the Color Registration Auto Adj. 3. Perform the Gamma Automatic Adjustment. <When abnormality occurs during the Color Registration Auto Adj. operation> 1. Execute the IO Check (99-70) of the board self-diagnosis. Check the results of IPB and the writing unit/Y (laser drive board/Y (LASDB/Y)). • When the result of IPB is NG: There is an abnormality in IPB or the connection. Go on to the step 5. • When the result of the writing unit/Y is NG: There is an abnormality in LASDB/Y or the connection. Go on to the following steps. 2. Prior check • Close the process door properly. • Close the front door properly. (Check with the IO Check (25-20) of the front door sensor (PS001).) • The color registration auto adjustment is completed normally. 3. Check the connector connection between IPB and LASDB/Y, CN1100 and CN1200 of IPB, CN200 (Relay connector), CN181 and CN180 of LASDB/Y, and the wiring. Then, repair it when there is any abnormality. 4. Replace the writing unit/Y. 5. Replace IPB. <When abnormality occurs during the output operation> 1. Check the connector connection of NVRAM (CN101), and repair it when there is any abnormality. 2. Replace NVRAM. <When the malfunction code occurs during the first printing after you changed the adjustment value of the Beam Pitch Adjustment> 1. When you input an inappropriate large value (example: +50, -100) to the Beam Pitch Adjustment: Configure the adjustment value of the Beam Pitch Adjustment to 0 once. Then, perform the Beam Pitch Adjustment again with the correct procedure (using the test chart). 2. When you input an appropriate value to the Beam Pitch Adjustment with the correct procedure (using the test chart): Replace the writing unit/Y.",
